- <b>The claimable predicate.</b> An event is claimable when its status is <code>pending</code>, <code>not_before</code> has passed, it is not claimed by a <code>running</code> run under a live lease, and one of these is true:
  - its thread has no open deferred call;
  - it <b>resolves</b> that thread's open call: an approval reply that matches an open <code>call_id</code>, the call's expiry timer event, or a user message on that thread (see (g), "superseded").

